        // A Pinch-fusion Warhead leaving its silo. The containment spinning up: deep throbs
        // coming faster and harder (never evenly) over a rough growl filling the cell. Then
        // the warhead goes: a deep plasmeric thump and crack, and the drive's roar, a dark
        // rough buzz torn by a fast flutter and a fizz, going away up and sinking. Not a
        // solid motor: no crackle. Every player hears the same sound.
